{
  "voice": "en-US-AndrewNeural",
  "rate": "-5%",
  "count": 35,
  "clips": [
    {
      "id": "s0b0",
      "index": 0,
      "screen": 0,
      "beat": 0,
      "file": "narr-00.mp3",
      "text": "Hi Jamie. We optimized your dashboard to improve the business. Isaac and I are running this as a proof of concept. You just watch.",
      "bytes": 49824,
      "voice": "en-US-AndrewNeural",
      "rate": "-5%"
    },
    {
      "id": "s1b0",
      "index": 1,
      "screen": 1,
      "beat": 0,
      "file": "narr-01.mp3",
      "text": "Here's the problem. 1,626 open jobs. And $138,467.50 owed on finished work. Too much is sitting on people.",
      "bytes": 76608,
      "voice": "en-US-AndrewNeural",
      "rate": "-5%"
    },
    {
      "id": "s2b0",
      "index": 2,
      "screen": 2,
      "beat": 0,
      "file": "narr-02.mp3",
      "text": "Meet the project bots. One per job, with a hard hat. They do the legwork.",
      "bytes": 45648,
      "voice": "en-US-AndrewNeural",
      "rate": "-5%"
    },
    {
      "id": "s2b1",
      "index": 3,
      "screen": 2,
      "beat": 1,
      "file": "narr-03.mp3",
      "text": "Above them, two supervisors. One for saunas, one for cellars. They rank the jobs.",
      "bytes": 37872,
      "voice": "en-US-AndrewNeural",
      "rate": "-5%"
    },
    {
      "id": "s2b2",
      "index": 4,
      "screen": 2,
      "beat": 2,
      "file": "narr-04.mp3",
      "text": "The GM bot sees both sides, and runs the shared crews.",
      "bytes": 25200,
      "voice": "en-US-AndrewNeural",
      "rate": "-5%"
    },
    {
      "id": "s2b3",
      "index": 5,
      "screen": 2,
      "beat": 3,
      "file": "narr-05.mp3",
      "text": "And on top, Isaac and me. People make the calls.",
      "bytes": 20160,
      "voice": "en-US-AndrewNeural",
      "rate": "-5%"
    },
    {
      "id": "s2b4",
      "index": 6,
      "screen": 2,
      "beat": 4,
      "file": "narr-06.mp3",
      "text": "Watch the lines. Solid means a plan going up. Dashed is a question or answer. Red is an escalation.",
      "bytes": 44208,
      "voice": "en-US-AndrewNeural",
      "rate": "-5%"
    },
    {
      "id": "s3b0",
      "index": 7,
      "screen": 3,
      "beat": 0,
      "file": "narr-07.mp3",
      "text": "The bots can look at JobTread, QuickBooks, Slack, Outlook, and the crew sheet. They can look, but they can't change anything.",
      "bytes": 49248,
      "voice": "en-US-AndrewNeural",
      "rate": "-5%"
    },
    {
      "id": "s4b0",
      "index": 8,
      "screen": 4,
      "beat": 0,
      "file": "narr-08.mp3",
      "text": "Story one. Salt Creek is booked twice. Job 7258 flags it. Watch the message climb to the supervisor.",
      "bytes": 51408,
      "voice": "en-US-AndrewNeural",
      "rate": "-5%"
    },
    {
      "id": "s4b1",
      "index": 9,
      "screen": 4,
      "beat": 1,
      "file": "narr-09.mp3",
      "text": "Job 7227 can't see other jobs, so it asks: is Salt Creek free for my racking?",
      "bytes": 38160,
      "voice": "en-US-AndrewNeural",
      "rate": "-5%"
    },
    {
      "id": "s4b2",
      "index": 10,
      "screen": 4,
      "beat": 2,
      "file": "narr-10.mp3",
      "text": "Job 6248 answers honestly. It's not install-ready.",
      "bytes": 26784,
      "voice": "en-US-AndrewNeural",
      "rate": "-5%"
    },
    {
      "id": "s4b3",
      "index": 11,
      "screen": 4,
      "beat": 3,
      "file": "narr-11.mp3",
      "text": "The sauna supervisor keeps 7258 on Salt Creek, and frees up 6248's slot.",
      "bytes": 47520,
      "voice": "en-US-AndrewNeural",
      "rate": "-5%"
    },
    {
      "id": "s4b4",
      "index": 12,
      "screen": 4,
      "beat": 4,
      "file": "narr-12.mp3",
      "text": "The cellar supervisor can't fix a clash across both sides. So it goes up to the GM, in red.",
      "bytes": 39456,
      "voice": "en-US-AndrewNeural",
      "rate": "-5%"
    },
    {
      "id": "s4b5",
      "index": 13,
      "screen": 4,
      "beat": 5,
      "file": "narr-13.mp3",
      "text": "The GM sees both sides. Salt Creek is on two jobs at once.",
      "bytes": 28224,
      "voice": "en-US-AndrewNeural",
      "rate": "-5%"
    },
    {
      "id": "s4b6",
      "index": 14,
      "screen": 4,
      "beat": 6,
      "file": "narr-14.mp3",
      "text": "Its plan: 7258 keeps Salt Creek. 7227's racking slides to November 4th, and still finishes before its promise.",
      "bytes": 69264,
      "voice": "en-US-AndrewNeural",
      "rate": "-5%"
    },
    {
      "id": "s4b7",
      "index": 15,
      "screen": 4,
      "beat": 7,
      "file": "narr-15.mp3",
      "text": "Every plan lines up. But nothing changes yet.",
      "bytes": 19728,
      "voice": "en-US-AndrewNeural",
      "rate": "-5%"
    },
    {
      "id": "s4b8",
      "index": 16,
      "screen": 4,
      "beat": 8,
      "file": "narr-16.mp3",
      "text": "The GM sends me the plan in Slack, and waits for my yes.",
      "bytes": 24480,
      "voice": "en-US-AndrewNeural",
      "rate": "-5%"
    },
    {
      "id": "s5b0",
      "index": 17,
      "screen": 5,
      "beat": 0,
      "file": "narr-17.mp3",
      "text": "Story two. Suceava is due Tuesday. On my visit, the cabinet was blocking the sprinkler head. That's life safety.",
      "bytes": 49104,
      "voice": "en-US-AndrewNeural",
      "rate": "-5%"
    },
    {
      "id": "s5b1",
      "index": 18,
      "screen": 5,
      "beat": 1,
      "file": "narr-18.mp3",
      "text": "The bot asks Isaac in Slack: who's our sprinkler contractor? It's not in JobTread yet.",
      "bytes": 34560,
      "voice": "en-US-AndrewNeural",
      "rate": "-5%"
    },
    {
      "id": "s5b2",
      "index": 19,
      "screen": 5,
      "beat": 2,
      "file": "narr-19.mp3",
      "text": "The cellar supervisor ranks this job number one. Safety comes first.",
      "bytes": 28656,
      "voice": "en-US-AndrewNeural",
      "rate": "-5%"
    },
    {
      "id": "s5b3",
      "index": 20,
      "screen": 5,
      "beat": 3,
      "file": "narr-20.mp3",
      "text": "It can hold the invoice, but it can't move a customer date. So it goes up to the GM.",
      "bytes": 31392,
      "voice": "en-US-AndrewNeural",
      "rate": "-5%"
    },
    {
      "id": "s5b4",
      "index": 21,
      "screen": 5,
      "beat": 4,
      "file": "narr-21.mp3",
      "text": "The GM proposes: move the date until the sprinkler is fixed, and hold the final invoice.",
      "bytes": 36288,
      "voice": "en-US-AndrewNeural",
      "rate": "-5%"
    },
    {
      "id": "s5b5",
      "index": 22,
      "screen": 5,
      "beat": 5,
      "file": "narr-22.mp3",
      "text": "Two calls go to people. The money call comes to me. The ops call goes to Isaac.",
      "bytes": 29376,
      "voice": "en-US-AndrewNeural",
      "rate": "-5%"
    },
    {
      "id": "s6b0",
      "index": 23,
      "screen": 6,
      "beat": 0,
      "file": "narr-23.mp3",
      "text": "Story three. Wespac is marked done, but the heater may never have been hooked up.",
      "bytes": 33120,
      "voice": "en-US-AndrewNeural",
      "rate": "-5%"
    },
    {
      "id": "s6b1",
      "index": 24,
      "screen": 6,
      "beat": 1,
      "file": "narr-24.mp3",
      "text": "And $4,728.58 is overdue. The bot can't answer that from JobTread, so it hands it up.",
      "bytes": 51840,
      "voice": "en-US-AndrewNeural",
      "rate": "-5%"
    },
    {
      "id": "s6b2",
      "index": 25,
      "screen": 6,
      "beat": 2,
      "file": "narr-25.mp3",
      "text": "The supervisor tries the crews. Burnstad is booked, APL is out, and there's no electrician on file.",
      "bytes": 42480,
      "voice": "en-US-AndrewNeural",
      "rate": "-5%"
    },
    {
      "id": "s6b3",
      "index": 26,
      "screen": 6,
      "beat": 3,
      "file": "narr-26.mp3",
      "text": "No answer yet. Watch the four-hour timer run down.",
      "bytes": 20880,
      "voice": "en-US-AndrewNeural",
      "rate": "-5%"
    },
    {
      "id": "s6b4",
      "index": 27,
      "screen": 6,
      "beat": 4,
      "file": "narr-27.mp3",
      "text": "The timer ran out, so it didn't wait. It escalated on its own.",
      "bytes": 26352,
      "voice": "en-US-AndrewNeural",
      "rate": "-5%"
    },
    {
      "id": "s6b5",
      "index": 28,
      "screen": 6,
      "beat": 5,
      "file": "narr-28.mp3",
      "text": "The GM asks Isaac to check with Burnstad: is the sauna running?",
      "bytes": 26352,
      "voice": "en-US-AndrewNeural",
      "rate": "-5%"
    },
    {
      "id": "s6b6",
      "index": 29,
      "screen": 6,
      "beat": 6,
      "file": "narr-29.mp3",
      "text": "Once Isaac confirms, I decide on sending Wespac the statement.",
      "bytes": 25200,
      "voice": "en-US-AndrewNeural",
      "rate": "-5%"
    },
    {
      "id": "s7b0",
      "index": 30,
      "screen": 7,
      "beat": 0,
      "file": "narr-30.mp3",
      "text": "People stay in charge. I make the money calls and give the final yes. Isaac runs day-to-day ops. Nothing happens without a human yes.",
      "bytes": 53856,
      "voice": "en-US-AndrewNeural",
      "rate": "-5%"
    },
    {
      "id": "s8b0",
      "index": 31,
      "screen": 8,
      "beat": 0,
      "file": "narr-31.mp3",
      "text": "A normal day. Bots sweep every job at 7. Isaac answers their questions, about 30 minutes. I approve in batches. You get a short weekly result.",
      "bytes": 60480,
      "voice": "en-US-AndrewNeural",
      "rate": "-5%"
    },
    {
      "id": "s9b0",
      "index": 32,
      "screen": 9,
      "beat": 0,
      "file": "narr-32.mp3",
      "text": "We start safe. Two weeks, read-only. The bots only suggest, and we check every suggestion.",
      "bytes": 41184,
      "voice": "en-US-AndrewNeural",
      "rate": "-5%"
    },
    {
      "id": "s10b0",
      "index": 33,
      "screen": 10,
      "beat": 0,
      "file": "narr-33.mp3",
      "text": "All we need from you, Jamie: your blessing for a two-week, read-only proof of concept, and OK for read-only access to QuickBooks and Slack. That's it.",
      "bytes": 63648,
      "voice": "en-US-AndrewNeural",
      "rate": "-5%"
    },
    {
      "id": "s11b0",
      "index": 34,
      "screen": 11,
      "beat": 0,
      "file": "narr-34.mp3",
      "text": "That's the whole team. Tap anyone to meet them. Every bot proposes. Isaac and I decide.",
      "bytes": 35712,
      "voice": "en-US-AndrewNeural",
      "rate": "-5%"
    }
  ],
